      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 70-year-old man was successfully operated on A-C bypass for coronary triple vessel disease and replacement of abdominal aortic aneurysm. The two different procedures were performed simultaneously under cardio-pulmonary bypass. This simultaneous operation can provide benefits of shortening operating time and of clamping easily the abdominal aorta."},
